      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The explicit algorithm supports accent folding, Unicode casefold expansion and interior substring matching. Event 26 executed it through rows obtained from the application connection and returned IDs 1 and 3 for cafe/afe, ID 2 for STRASSE, and no matches for xyz or empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "U2",
      "quote": "Return exact original tuples, no deduplication or fuzzy ranking; 5000-row workload exact ascending odd IDs; no latency SLA.",
      "locator": "plans[0].final.work_items[0].context",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The design selects original ID/title tuples with ORDER BY id and uses ephemeral comparison keys. Duplicate titles retain separate IDs. The standard-library scan fits the stated offline, in-memory scope; event 26 also observed unchanged titles and the exact ordered 5000-row result."
    },
    {
      "id": "U3",
      "quote": "normalized-scan 'cafe' [(1, 'Café Racer'), (3, 'Café Racer')]\nnormalized-scan 'STRASSE' [(2, 'Die Straße')]\nnormalized-scan 'afe' [(1, 'Café Racer'), (3, 'Café Racer')]\nnormalized-scan 'xyz' []\nnormalized-scan '' []",
      "locator": "application_tool_evidence, event 26, completed probe output",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The executed probe used src.database.connect, explicit independently specified expected tuples and reversed insertion order. Its exit status was zero. Together with the supplied adapter source and explicit local algorithm, this supports the selected mechanism without inferring semantics from SQLite's version. The failed LIKE/default-trigram observations are appropriately limited to those tested configurations."
    },
    {
      "id": "U4",
      "quote": "Call the public API for cafe, STRASSE, afe, xyz and empty string.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, RBC-1",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "The plan retains component checks through the application connection and a Python consumer procedure using the actual seed and public API, with exact tuples, repeated calls and preservation checks. Additional planned cases cover normalization, literal punctuation, capacity and visible database failures. Existing baseline/full-suite regression remains required. These checks are explicitly unexecuted; a CLI is not required by the stated request."
    },
    {
      "id": "U5",
      "quote": "Maximum 5000 titles makes a linear scan appropriate without indexes, external services or new dependencies.",
      "locator": "planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, AD-2",
      "grade": 2,
      "reason": "One local search increment is proportionate to the bounded catalog. The plan avoids an elaborate search subsystem and stops investigating alternative FTS configurations once a compatible mechanism is established. Schema/API choices are explicit future implementation obligations, with correction before dependent work if incompatible; no unresolved external feasibility boundary is concealed."
